BT 1 0 0 1 0 49 Tm .47253 Tw 14.5 TL /F1 9 Tf .066667 .094118 .152941 rg (Planck-99 is a deterministic, integer-only binary classifier that ingests a host-level syscall trace and returns a single) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.117835 Tw (verdict: ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (Malware) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( or ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (Benign) Tj /F1 9 Tf (. It is compiled to a standalone C header \227 no runtime, no interpreter, no OS calls \227 and) Tj T* 0 Tw .963729 Tw (runs entirely in userspace with zero floating-point operations and zero external dependencies. Every classification) Tj T* 0 Tw (produces a JSON audit trail with the full decision path.) Tj T* ET
